1
00:04:40,909 --> 00:04:46,909
When your Dad's an undertaker, your Mom's in heaven, and your Grandma's got a screw
loose...it's good to have a friend who understands you. Even if he is a boy.

2
00:09:21,818 --> 00:09:27,818
My Girl is a comedy, drama film directed by Howard Zieff.

3
00:14:02,727 --> 00:14:08,727
Vada Sultenfuss is obsessed with death.

4
00:18:43,636 --> 00:18:49,636
Her mother is dead, and her father runs a funeral parlor.

5
00:23:24,545 --> 00:23:30,545
She is also in love with her English teacher, and joins a
poetry class over the summer just to impress him.

6
00:28:05,454 --> 00:28:11,454
Thomas J., her best friend, is "allergic to everything",
and sticks with Vada despite her hangups.

7
00:32:46,363 --> 00:32:52,363
When Vada's father hires Shelly, and begins to fall for
her, things take a turn to the worse...

8
00:37:27,272 --> 00:37:33,272
Vada Sultenfuss, played by Anna Chlumsky.

9
00:42:08,181 --> 00:42:14,181
Thomas J. Sennett, played by Macaulay Culkin.

10
00:46:49,090 --> 00:46:55,090
Harry Sultenfuss, played by Dan Aykroyd.

11
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Shelly DeVoto, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

12
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:16,909
Phil Sultenfuss, played by Richard Masur.

13
01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
Mr. Jake Bixler, played by Griffin Dunne.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
My Girl is a 1991 American coming-of-age romantic comedy-drama film directed by Howard Zieff, written by Laurice Elehwany, and
starring Dan Aykroyd, Jamie Lee Curtis, Macaulay Culkin, and Anna Chlumsky in her first role in a major motion picture.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
A book based on the film was written by Patricia Hermes.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
The film tells the story of an 11-year-old girl living in
Madison, Pennsylvania, during the summer of 1972.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
The film's title refers to the classic 1964 song of the same name by The
Temptations, which is also featured in the film's end credits.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
The film was released by Columbia Pictures on November 27, 1991,
and grossed $121 million on a budget of $17 million.

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
A sequel, My Girl 2, was released in 1994.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film explores themes of friendship, 1970s, beehive, remarriage, neighbor.

21
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:25,090
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
